{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_REDACTEDsessionid0001", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "available_commands_update", "availableCommands": [{"name": "a11y-widget-body-star-overrides-headings", "description": "Diagnose and fix design-system typography that silently never applies because\nan accessibility/user-preference stylesheet sets the same property on\n`body, body *`. Use when: (1) a rule like `h1, h2 { letter-spacing: -0.015em }`\nhas no effect and computed style reports `normal`, (2) only PART of a rule\nblock applies \u2014 e.g. `text-wrap: balance` works but `letter-spacing` does not,\n(3) the project ships an accessibility widget / font-size / spacing controls\n(a11y.css, accessibility-toolbar, userway-style panel), (4) DevTools shows\nyour declaration struck through by a `body *` rule you did not write. Root\ncause: `body *` and a bare `h1` have EQUAL specificity (0,0,1), so the later\nstylesheet in source order wins \u2014 and the a11y sheet is injected after the\nmain one. Covers the correct fix: raise specificity to `body h1` AND compose\nwith the a11y variable via calc() so the user's accessibility control keeps\nworking instead of being hard-overridden.\n"}, {"name": "actioncable-single-use-ticket-auth", "description": "Authenticate an ActionCable WebSocket with a short-lived, single-use ticket\ninstead of a long-lived JWT/token in the connection URL, WITHOUT breaking\nauto-reconnect. Use when: (1) security review flags \"secrets/JWT in URL\" for a\n`/cable?token=<jwt>` handshake, (2) you must replace a URL-borne credential\nwith a one-time ticket but the consumer is long-lived and auto-reconnects,\n(3) a naive \"fetch ticket then createConsumer(url)\" works on first connect but\nthe socket dies permanently after the ticket's TTL because reconnects reuse\nthe consumed/expired ticket. Covers the Redis-backed single-use ticket store\n(atomic GET+DEL) and the reconnect-safe synchronous URL-function pattern for\n@rails/actioncable.\n"}, {"...": "248 more commands elided for fixture size"}]}}}
